Write a program that reads an XML document from standard input and prints the equivalent nested dictionary as JSON on standard output.

Input format:
- The entire input is one XML document.

Output format:
- The conventional XML-to-dictionary mapping, printed as JSON indented by 2 spaces: child tag names become keys, attribute names get a leading "@", text that coexists with attributes or children goes under "#text", repeated sibling tags become lists, keys in document order.
- If the input is not well-formed XML, print exactly: Error: invalid XML

Example:
Input:
<root><a x="1">hi</a><a>there</a></root>

Output:
{
  "root": {
    "a": [
      {
        "@x": "1",
        "#text": "hi"
      },
      "there"
    ]
  }
}

